        <generalfeedback format="html">
            <text><![CDATA[
<p>
    <span class="multilang" lang="en">
        The general form of the sinusoidal function is \( y = A \sin(\omega t +\alpha), \omega&gt;0. \)
    </span>
    <span class="multilang" lang="no">
        Den generelle formen for den sinusformede funksjonen er \( y = A \sin(\omega t +\alpha), \omega&gt;0. \)
    </span>
    <span class="multilang" lang="de">
        Die allgemeine Form der Sinusfunktion ist \( y = A \sin(\omega t +\alpha), \omega&gt;0. \)
    </span>
</p>
<p>
    <span class="multilang" lang="en">
        We are given the functions:
    </span>
    <span class="multilang" lang="no">
        Vi får funksjonene:
    </span>
    <span class="multilang" lang="de">
        Uns werden die Funktionen gegeben:
    </span>
</p>
<p>
</p>
<p>
    \(A: y = {@pr_funcs[1]@}\)
</p>
<p>
    \(B: y = {@pr_funcs[2]@} \)
    <br/>
</p>
<p>
    \(C: y = {@pr_funcs[3]@} \)
    <br/>
</p>
<p>
    \(D: y ={@pr_funcs[4]@} \)
</p>
<span class="multilang" lang="en">
    We start with the function \( y = {@a*sin(w*t)@} \) which has amplitude \( A = {@a@} \), \( \omega = {@w@}\) and period \( T = \frac{2 \pi}{\omega} = {@T@} = {@dispdp(float(T),2)@}. \)
</span>
<span class="multilang" lang="no">
    Vi starter med funksjonen \( y = {@a*sin(w*t)@} \) som har amplitude \( A = {@a@} \), \( \omega = {@w@}\) og periode \( T = \frac{2 \pi}{\omega} = {@T@} = {@dispdp(float(T),2)@}. \)
</span>
<span class="multilang" lang="de">
    Wir beginnen mit der Funktion \( y = {@a*sin(w*t)@} \) mit der Amplitude \( A = {@a@} \) , \( \omega = {@w@}\) und Periode \( T = \frac{2 \pi}{\omega} = {@T@} = {@dispdp(float(T),2)@} . \)
</span>
<p>
    <span class="multilang" lang="en">
        The graph of \( y = {@a*sin(w*t+phi)@}\) is obtained by moving the graph of \( y = {@a*sin(w*t)@} \) horizontally to the left by {@phi@} units.
        <br/>
        The function \( y = {@(a/2)*sin(w*t)@} \) has \( A = {@a/2@} \), \( \omega = {@w@}\) and period \( T = \frac{2 \pi}{\omega} = {@T@} = {@dispdp(float(T),2)@}. \)
    </span>
    <span class="multilang" lang="no">
        Grafen til \( y = {@a*sin(w*t+phi)@}\) fås ved å flytte grafen til \( y = {@a*sin(w*t)@} \) horisontalt til venstre med {@phi@} enheter.
        <br/>
        Funksjonen \( y = {@(a/2)*sin(w*t)@} \) har \( A = {@a/2@} \), \( \omega = {@w @}\) og periode \( T = \frac{2 \pi}{\omega} = {@T@} = {@dispdp(float(T),2)@}. \)
    </span>
    <span class="multilang" lang="de">
        Der Graph von \( y = {@a*sin(w*t+phi)@}\) wird durch Verschieben des Graphen von \( y = {@a *sin(w*t)@} \) horizontal um {@phi@} Einheiten nach links erhalten.
        <br/>
        Die Funktion \( y = {@(a/2)*sin(w*t)@} \) hat \( A = {@a/2@} \), \( \omega = {@w @}\) und Periode \( T = \frac{2 \pi}{\omega} = {@T@} = {@dispdp(float(T),2)@}. \)
    </span>
</p>
<p>
    <span class="multilang" lang="en">
        Finally, the function \( y = {@a*sin(w/2*t)@} \) has \( A = {@a@} \), \( \omega = {@w/2@}\) and period \( T = \frac{2 \pi}{\omega} = {@2*T@} = {@dispdp(float(2*T),2)@}. \)
    </span>
    <span class="multilang" lang="no">
        Til slutt har funksjonen \( y = {@a*sin(w/2*t)@} \) \( A = {@a@} \), \( \omega = {@w/2@}\) og periode \( T = \frac{2 \pi}{\omega} = {@2*T@} = {@dispdp(float(2*T),2)@}. \)
    </span>
    <span class="multilang" lang="de">
        Schließlich hat die Funktion \( y = {@a*sin(w/2*t)@} \) \( A = {@a@} \), \( \omega = {@w/2@}\) und Periode \( T = \frac{2 \pi}{\omega} = {@2*T@} = {@dispdp(float(2*T) ,2)@}. \)
    </span>
</p>
]]></text>
